    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the previously-failing `Cp23Tests` (tier-gold) and the unchanged `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` is derived at read time on the `Owner` entity from *stored* fields (like `namesakeCount`). To support GOLD I recorded the household size at create time (mirroring how `namesakeCount` is a create-time snapshot) and extended the derivation.\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a stored `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with accessors, and a GOLD branch first in `getMembershipTier()`: returns `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n2. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new pipeline function) \u2014 after `AssignHousehold` stamps the shared `householdId`, it counts the members: `1` for the not-yet-saved new owner plus every stored owner with the same non-null `householdId`. A household-less owner (`householdId == null`) is a household of one.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `household-size` step (under `transaction` governance) between `household-assign` and `registrationDate`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"householdSize\", ignore = true)` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, consistent with the other pipeline-assigned fields.\n\n5. **Schema** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to the owners table in all four DB scripts (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nFor the tested scenario (three owners sharing last name + address with `sharesHousehold=true`): the third create sees the two already-stamped household members plus itself \u2192 size 3 \u2192 GOLD, while the earlier members keep their base tier \u2014 matching \"3 or more members **after this create**.\"",
